# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# TRL — environment variable template
#
# STATUS: TRL CURRENTLY REQUIRES NO SECRETS.
#
# This repository is a static site with no server, no database, and no
# third-party API calls. Nothing here is needed to run or deploy it.
#
# This file exists to set the pattern BEFORE the first secret ever appears,
# so no one improvises when it does. See docs/TRL_SECURITY.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# RULES
#   1. PLACEHOLDERS ONLY in this file. Never a real value — not even an
#      expired or revoked one.
#   2. Real values go in `.env`, which is gitignored. Never commit it.
#   3. A static site has NO private runtime. Anything reaching script.js is
#      public. A real secret requires a server or serverless function.
#   4. If a credential is ever committed: ROTATE IT FIRST, then purge history.
#      Rewriting history without rotating is theatre.

# --- Local preview (optional) -----------------------------------
# Port for `python3 -m http.server`. Not a secret; convenience only.
# PORT=8000

# --- Future: form backend (only if D-004 is revisited at Gate 3) --
# Endpoint for a third-party form service. Public by nature, but keep it
# configurable so it is never hardcoded across pages.
# PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT=https://example.com/f/your-form-id

# --- Future: analytics (would require a privacy.html update) ------
# Adding analytics changes TRL's privacy posture. If this is ever set,
# docs/TRL_SECURITY.md §7 and privacy.html MUST be updated in the same commit.
# PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_ID=placeholder-not-a-real-id

# --- NOT secrets — do not move these here -------------------------
# The WhatsApp number and TRL email addresses are published business contact
# details (decision D-009). They belong in the HTML. Moving them to env vars
# would break every call-to-action on the site.
